We perform the polynomial division: \[
\begin{array}{c|cc cc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{5x} & +4 \\
\cline{2-5}
2x^2-3x+1 & 10x^3&-7x^2&+ax&+6   \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{-10x^3} & +15x^2 & -5x \\
\cline{2-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & 8x^2 & (a-5)x & 6 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & -8x^2 & +12x & -4 \\
\cline{3-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & 0 & (a-5+12)x & 2 \\
\end{array}
\]The remainder will be constant if and only if $a-5+12=0.$ So $a = \boxed{-7}.$

Begin by distributing in the innermost parentheses: \begin{align*}
\left(2x+\frac{3}{2} (4x-6)\right)-&4\left( -(2-x)+\frac{x}{2}\right)\\
&=(2x+6x-9)-4\left(-2+x+\frac{x}{2}\right)\\
&=(8x-9)-4\left (-2+\frac{3x}{2}\right)
\end{align*} Now, distribute again, and combine like terms: \begin{align*}
(8x-9)-4\left (-2+\frac{3x}{2}\right)&=8x-9+8-6x\\
&=\boxed{2x-1}
\end{align*}

We can expand the determinant as follows:
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} 0 & b - a & c - a \\ a - b & 0 & c - b \\ a - c & b - c & 0 \end{vmatrix} &= -(b - a) \begin{vmatrix} a - b & c - b \\ a - c & 0 \end{vmatrix} + (c - a) \begin{vmatrix} a - b & 0 \\ a - c & b - c \end{vmatrix} \\
&= -(b - a)(-(c - b)(a - c)) + (c - a)(a - b)(b - c) \\
&= \boxed{0}.
\end{align*}

